			<div class="content" id="post-content-4607501">
									

This may be the best SCP on the site if ever read. I reread the entire thing until I finally feel that I have a moderate understanding. So here we go! (Also quick warning for spelling and grammar errors)<br />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>There is an entity in the minds of every human that is not naturally occurring and is responsible for pain, suffering, ect. SCP-682 possess knowledge about this entity and this explains it's desire to fuck over the human race.<br />
The Overseer Council and ethics agree that is would be a mercy to kill all humans compared to what this entity has in mind.<br />
SCP-682 either finds a way to take a human body or comes into contact with a mimetic agent that makes it seem like he's a human. He was then interrogated and forms back into his normal shape and eats them. What made me think he ate them was the line at the end, &quot;Distrusting&quot;. All the references to 682 work very well as to not make the reader shrug off the article for including the classic. I know I'm getting a little off topic but the part about where he's listing anomalies that have been turned on the humans and you see some famous scips like 097 and 662, and you know what's coming next, &quot;SCP-682 | Released&quot; That one word sent chills up my spine. Anyway I'll get back onto topic.<br />
055 + 579 = Restart time to before the crisis happened.<br />
Our hero manages to reset the timeline but heroically sacrifices himself to the good of humanity&#8230; But wait, if the Overseers and Ethics agreed that this was a mercy, does that now mean humans are headed straight for whatever is worse than Plagues, Blunt force trauma, a giant fucking lizard, and memetic kill agents, then the world is on a highway to hell.<br />
I loved this piece and I think it also helped the lore for 579, 055 and, 682. They didn't really need help but I feel like now 682 isn't just a lizard that fucking hates humans, it may be he's trying to save them, and is pissed because we don't realize he's saving us, I also made a connection to 049, is this the true pestilence? I think this is underrated even at 4 digits. Also all the other series-1 anomalies didn't make me cringe, it was actually exiting to see them in there, I'm getting repetitive so here's my two cents, Best. Article. Ever.</p>
</div>
</div>
