<p>I actually have an alternate theory based on the fact that this thing didn’t seem to effect the entirety of humanity and 05-1’s comment “to think I’d find myself agreeing with that damn lizard”. I think that whatever they found wasn’t scp-682, but rather is the reason why scp-682 finds us so repulsive. When they found this thing they were repulsed too, as whatever it is is something truly abominable. The file they sent out was the cure, and the what became of the members of the foundation was the result of curing them of this thing. When they were cured they were released from its influence, and they saw the rest of humanity the same way scp-682 does, <em>disgusting</em>. and so driven by this newfound hatred for “real” humans they decided to kill them all, rather than try and cure them too.<br />
As for what this thing is I have a theory. It’s humanity itself, in the metaphysical sense anyway. It’s something that is integral in the human psyche, making us what we are. When the foundation cured themselves they removed their humanity, so much so that anomalies that effect humans didn’t effect them anymore</p>
