<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I’ve always found it kind of interesting that 682 has a hatred of all life despite it being alive. That being said, in some ways it isn’t really alive. As in, it’s an immortal being, and one of the key driving factors of life is mortality, it’s the basis of our entire moral system and it’s the basis of how we decide to live our lives. I’ve always just seen this as a flaw in the 682 article, and frankly, I think the whole 682 article really is just a fever dream. But I think the thing being removed is empathy, the moment they no longer fear death, is the moment they can no longer feel other’s pain. Or maybe there’s something I’m not grasping here. Something inherent that makes people human that was removed from everyone in the Foundation and isn’t present in 682. But I’m not sure.</p>
