<p>3125 doesn't work like that at all though. When 3125 fully enters a universe, there's no more room for any kind of thoughts that <em>aren't</em> 3125. It's literally impossible to think about anything else. There's no freeing yourself from it because there's nowhere to run. Anyone who is possessed (save for a precious few people like Adam Wheeler who are naturally resistant) is permanently overwritten and can be considered effectively dead. There's no freeing themselves or coming back. Ever.</p>
<p>In the latest Antimemetics Division stories, 3125 <em>has</em> won, and from a mental/informational perspective, there's nothing left in the universe but it. The Foundation, all the groups of interest, sentient and non-sentient SCP objects, all were either destroyed in a matter of hours or buried under so much antimemetic censoring that they have become invisible and irrelevant.</p>

