<p>This whole scenario feels like Bart Hughes' first off the cuff proposal for killing 3125. Destroy the entire human race so that it can't exist.</p>
<p>The 0-5 and Tejani agree with that damned lizard, which isn't too dissimilar from the way that Adam sees all of the other people when he's the only one who isn't controlled by వ. More than that, when Ross tells the people in Ganzir something, they die in a grisly fashion, which isn't too different from what's implied to happen to people who comprehend the existence of 3125.</p>
<p>Whatever the case, the Foundation's decision and goal isn't different from what Bart suggested. To destroy IT, they have to destroy every single human being, and for whatever reason they decide that's what they have to do.</p>
